# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# cppclip — what git should and should not carry
#
# The rule this file follows: track what a reader needs to *check* the claims,
# ignore what a reader can *regenerate*.  Source, the result tables behind every
# quoted number, and the figures the documents embed are tracked, because
# without them the write-up cannot be verified without re-running a 50-minute
# pipeline.  Virtual environments, datasets, container images and the raw
# exchanged solutions are ignored: they are large, reproducible from a script
# or a DOI, and would bloat a clone to over a gigabyte.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Python -----------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/
pip-wheel-metadata/
MANIFEST

# --- virtual environments ---------------------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
.venv*/
# NOTE: fields2cover's build workspace also lives here and is ignored further
# down under "Fields2Cover build artefacts" -- it is *not* a virtualenv.

# --- scratch space ----------------------------------------------------------
.tmp/

# --- tooling caches ---------------------------------------------------------
.pytest_cache/
.cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.pytype/
*.log

# --- test and coverage artefacts -------------------------------------------
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml
htmlcov/
.tox/
.nox/
.hypothesis/

# --- OS junk ----------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
desktop.ini

# --- editor junk ------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
*.orig
*.rej

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# What is deliberately NOT ignored
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# results/figures/  the report embeds these; without them it renders with broken
#                   images, and a reader cannot see the evidence without
#                   re-running a 50-minute pipeline.
# results/gui/      screenshots of the viewer, embedded in the READMEs.
# results/tables/   the condensed evidence behind every quoted number, and what
#                   experiments/audit_numbers.py checks the write-up against.
# notes/            the verified bibliography and the raw verification report.
# *.zh-CN.md        the Chinese editions of the README and the report; a
#                   translated document is a deliverable, not a build artefact.
# data/DATASETS.md  provenance and licences for data too large to vendor.
# .gitattributes    line-ending normalisation; without it a Windows and a Linux
#                   checkout disagree on every file.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- datasets ---------------------------------------------------------------
# 203 MB across 809 files, and separately licensed (113 of the Lithuanian fields
# are non-commercial-use-only).  DATASETS.md records the DOI and URL to re-fetch
# every one of them.
data/*
!data/DATASETS.md

# --- Fields2Cover build artefacts ------------------------------------------
# env/ holds the upstream source tree, the sdist, the container's tutorial
# output and the exploratory comparison scripts from building the baseline.
# tools/setup_fields2cover.sh rebuilds all of it from the ROS 2 deb.
env/
tools/out/
tools/ros.key
*.deb
*.tar.gz

# --- raw exchanged solutions for the head-to-head --------------------------
# 334 MB across 1053 JSON files.  Regenerable in about two minutes with
# experiments/export_cppclip.py plus the container sweep, and
# experiments/exp_compare.py reduces it to results/tables/exp4_compare.csv,
# which *is* tracked.
results/f2c_io/

# --- exploratory plots, not used by the report -----------------------------
# Produced by tools/render_figures.py while looking for a useful picture.  The
# figures the documents actually embed are tracked above.
results/figures/intervals.png
results/figures/plans_grid.png
results/figures/plan_rectilinear.png
